{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_tenant_pluggable_data_architecture", "label": "Tenant-Pluggable Data Architecture (five-boundary assessment)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/tenant-pluggable-data-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_tenant_pluggable_data_architecture_five_boundaries", "label": "Five-boundary frame (document acquisition, blob, relational, vector, business-DB query)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/tenant-pluggable-data-architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a70, \u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The five boundaries are not equally worth building; treating them as five instances of the same pattern is named as the main programme risk. Document acquisition and blob storage are small, high-value ports; relational persistence should be relocated, not abstracted; vector needs a reshaped existing protocol; business-DB query is a new retrieval capability, not an adapter."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_tenant_pluggable_data_architecture_p3_relational_relocation", "label": "P3 \u2014 Derived relational persistence: connection routing, not a repository abstraction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/tenant-pluggable-data-architecture.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 P3, \u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "entity_views.py generates DDL at runtime (CREATE TABLE/ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS), relational_projection.py uses ON CONFLICT/GREATEST upserts, and provisioning clones templates via pg_tables \u2014 a vendor-neutral abstraction would have to reproduce all of that per engine, which is 'a second product'; pointing the identical schema at a different PostgreSQL server is far cheaper and is the recommended path."}], "edges": [{"source": "doc